ld Mountain and Elk, Ferris, and\nBabylon burn scars to name a few.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoonal moisture will remain across the area through Monday\nevening and will support thunderstorms and showers with heavy\nrainfall across the watch area. Several rounds of heavier rain\nare expected increasing the chance for flash flooding especially\nin our more susceptible areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Central Yampa River Basin; Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley; Debeque to Silt Corridor; Central Colorado River Basin; Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre River Basin; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops; Upper Gunnison River Valley; Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Southeast Utah; Tavaputs Plateau; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f7ff695e018105cca90d3b4c59e6816f865c6d8a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f7ff695e018105cca90d3b4c59e6816f865c6d8a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-31T05:26:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 310526 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1126 PM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to widespread precipitation chances return Monday, with higher coverage of precipitation across southeast UT and southwest CO than previous days. - Flash Flooding will continue to be possible as organized and training thunderstorms can produce h","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-31T07:09:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Showers and thunderstorms are on tap again today with heavy 